00:19:09,481 --> 00:19:10,816
[Mary] Your work is almost done.

463
00:19:10,899 --> 00:19:12,150
[Sabrina] Perfect.

464
00:19:12,234 --> 00:19:15,320
[Sabrina and Mary chatting indistinctly]

465
00:19:15,404 --> 00:19:17,614
I feel like I should be in 
a Michael Jackson video.

466
00:19:19,158 --> 00:19:20,075
[Mary] Hey, Amanza?

467
00:19:21,159 --> 00:19:23,078
Christine's texting me.

468
00:19:23,162 --> 00:19:24,538
She wants to talk.

469
00:19:24,621 --> 00:19:26,707
Okay... [chuckles]

470
00:19:26,790 --> 00:19:28,959
[Mary] I told her I'm trying 
to do the dress fitting,

471
00:19:29,042 --> 00:19:32,671
so she might be stopping by 
to talk about last night.

472
00:19:32,754 --> 00:19:34,882
So she wants to come 
to your dress fitting?

473
00:19:34,965 --> 00:19:37,634
[Mary] I don't want any drama.
This whole thing is so stupid.

474
00:19:43,390 --> 00:19:45,976
-Does it-- Does it look good?
-Oh, yeah.

475
00:19:46,351 --> 00:19:47,978
You look absolutely stunning.

476
00:19:48,395 --> 00:19:49,396
Yay!

477
00:19:49,479 --> 00:19:52,191
It fits you like a glove. 
It's so beautiful.

478
00:19:54,234 --> 00:19:56,069
So she text me. She says

479
00:19:56,153 --> 00:19:58,572
that she wants to, like,
make things better

480
00:19:58,655 --> 00:20:01,200
-before the wedding, which I'd love.
-Oh, my God.

481
00:20:01,283 --> 00:20:02,910
[Amanza] That is so stupid.

482
00:20:02,993 --> 00:20:04,745
It was pure stripper pole fun.

483
00:20:04,828 --> 00:20:07,039
[Mary] Thank you, Amanza. Thank you.

484
00:20:07,122 --> 00:20:09,499
-[Amanza] I found my new side hustle.
-I want a stripper pole.

485
00:20:09,583 --> 00:20:12,252
I know, right? If real estate 
doesn't work out for me...

486
00:20:13,253 --> 00:20:15,088
A little extra walking around money.

487
00:20:15,172 --> 00:20:17,382
[cell phone vibrating]

488
00:20:21,053 --> 00:20:21,970
Christine's here.

489
00:20:24,473 --> 00:20:26,725
I'm gonna, um-- I'm gonna go get her.

490
00:20:28,226 --> 00:20:30,479
-I'll be right back.
-You got your boxing gloves on?

491
00:20:30,562 --> 00:20:32,648
[laughs] I don't need them, honey.

492
00:20:43,325 --> 00:20:45,077
[Christine] Hey, Amanza!

493
00:20:45,994 --> 00:20:47,746
[Amanza] Did you bring me flowers?

494
00:20:47,829 --> 00:20:49,915
[Christine] These are for Mary, actually.

495
00:20:49,998 --> 00:20:51,917
Are those real flowers
or are they clown flowers 

496
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:53,335
that you're gonna squirt water
in her face?

497
00:20:53,418 --> 00:20:55,128
What? No! Why would you say that?

498
00:20:55,212 --> 00:20:57,381
I came here to talk to her and apologize.

499
00:20:57,464 --> 00:21:00,175
I want her to have the best
for her wedding. That's why I'm here.

500
00:21:00,842 --> 00:21:05,055
Best movie ever, Kevin Costner, 
Whitney Houston, Bodyguard.

501
00:21:05,138 --> 00:21:06,848
And I'm getting major vibes of it

502
00:21:06,932 --> 00:21:09,643
because Amanza has become
Mary's bodyguard.

503
00:21:09,726 --> 00:21:11,937
It's like, no one can have a conversation
with her or talk to her 

504
00:21:12,020 --> 00:21:13,897
without her butting in 
or getting in the way.

505
00:21:13,981 --> 00:21:15,857
She doesn't have to be worried.
I'm here to apologize.

506
00:21:15,941 --> 00:21:18,485
I have flowers in my hand.
I'm not gonna punch her in the face.

507
00:21:18,568 --> 00:21:21,947
I don't feel good about the way that,
you know, last night happened,

508
00:21:22,030 --> 00:21:23,323
and I just want to make sure that

509
00:21:24,032 --> 00:21:26,827
her and I clear the air of everything,

510
00:21:26,910 --> 00:21:27,953
and apologize.

511
00:21:28,036 --> 00:21:29,037
Okay.

512
00:21:29,746 --> 00:21:33,125
[Amanza] Whatever you say better be nice 
because she's at her breaking point.

513
00:21:33,667 --> 00:21:34,918
No drama, I promise.

514
00:21:35,877 --> 00:21:37,254
I'll give you guys a minute.

515
00:21:37,337 --> 00:21:38,213
Thanks.

516
00:21:38,297 --> 00:21:40,716
[Christine gasps] Hi, babe!

517
00:21:40,841 --> 00:21:43,343
-Hey, how are you?
-[Christine] You look beautiful.

518
00:21:43,427 --> 00:21:44,594
Thank you.

519
00:21:44,678 --> 00:21:47,306
-I brought you flowers.
-Oh, thank you.

520
00:21:47,389 --> 00:21:50,350
I know this is a weird time
because you're really busy,

521
00:21:50,434 --> 00:21:54,479
but I did want to come here 
and apologize because I know

522
00:21:54,563 --> 00:21:56,773
things got a little 
out of hand last night.

523
00:21:57,149 --> 00:22:00,485
I want to apologize if I brought
everything up at the wrong time

524
00:22:00,569 --> 00:22:04,364
and I want to apologize 
for being a total bitch.

525
00:22:04,656 --> 00:22:05,490
Thank you.

526
00:22:05,907 --> 00:22:09,328
Forgive me if I hurt your feelings
in any way.

527
00:22:10,495 --> 00:22:14,916
What I realized last night
after I got home was that...

528
00:22:15,834 --> 00:22:19,504
"Wow, Mary and I actually 
haven't talked in so long."

529
00:22:19,588 --> 00:22:23,216
I haven't talked to you
since our fight at my listing.

530
00:22:23,508 --> 00:22:26,261
And it's been really hard 

531
00:22:26,345 --> 00:22:28,680
that I had to go the office

532
00:22:28,764 --> 00:22:32,392
where you and Chrishell
are talking about your dress fitting,

533
00:22:32,476 --> 00:22:34,561
and all these things
that I'm not getting invited to,

534
00:22:34,644 --> 00:22:37,147
so I'm feeling isolated.

535
00:22:37,522 --> 00:22:40,108
I lost my friend and I don't know why.

536
00:22:40,776 --> 00:22:44,446
There was no intention of ever trying
to hurt anybody's feelings.

537
00:22:44,905 --> 00:22:47,741
I've been busy with work and the wedding.

538
00:22:47,824 --> 00:22:49,242
You've been off traveling.

539
00:22:49,326 --> 00:22:52,329
Before, you were like, "No, we're cool."
So, when something happens,

540
00:22:52,412 --> 00:22:54,498
I'm like, "Okay, maybe we're not cool?"

541
00:22:54,581 --> 00:22:57,084
So when it comes to me and you,

542
00:22:57,167 --> 00:22:58,960
I agree that we do need to talk,

543
00:22:59,044 --> 00:23:01,421
but right now I'm days away
from my wedding.

544
00:23:02,130 --> 00:23:03,590
And I want my old friend back.

545
00:23:04,049 --> 00:23:06,718
-We should've just had a conversation.
-Right.

546
00:23:07,386 --> 00:23:08,845
[Mary] Please come to me.

547
00:23:08,929 --> 00:23:10,972
I don't want fights. 
I don't want constant,

548
00:23:11,056 --> 00:23:13,475
"Did you hear this?
Do you know what she said?"

549
00:23:13,558 --> 00:23:14,851
I feel stupid for that.

550
00:23:15,727 --> 00:23:16,561
Yeah.

551
00:23:16,645 --> 00:23:17,729
[Christine] From now on...

552
00:23:18,855 --> 00:23:22,192
let's just...
try to get back to where we were.

553
00:23:22,776 --> 00:23:23,735
We will.

554
00:23:23,819 --> 00:23:28,824
I think Christine is genuine
in her apology, but...

555
00:23:30,033 --> 00:23:31,243
I don't know. [sighs]

556
00:23:31,326 --> 00:23:34,704
I mean, things have gone 
up and down before,

557
00:23:34,788 --> 00:23:37,999
but I think she is and I hope she is

558
00:23:38,333 --> 00:23:39,751
because I miss my old girl.

559
00:23:40,168 --> 00:23:42,629
I want you to have
the most amazing wedding.

560
00:23:42,712 --> 00:23:43,547
[Mary] Yeah.

561
00:23:44,339 --> 00:23:45,715
A no-drama wedding.

562
00:23:56,435 --> 00:23:59,479
♪ Oh-oh
Woah-oh-oh-oh ♪

563
00:23:59,855 --> 00:24:04,317
♪ Oh-oh
Woah-oh-oh-oh ♪

564
00:24:04,401 --> 00:24:07,529
♪ I just wanna dive into the blue ♪

565
00:24:09,364 --> 00:24:11,992
♪ It doesn't really matter what we do ♪

566
00:24:13,827 --> 00:24:17,205
♪ Don't let the moment pass us by ♪

567
00:24:18,290 --> 00:24:21,251
♪ Just trust that the universe is right ♪

568
00:24:21,334 --> 00:24:22,878
-Come here.
-Uh, thank you.

569
00:24:22,961 --> 00:24:25,338
-You doing okay?
-I'm good, I'm good.

570
00:24:25,422 --> 00:24:26,590
-Yeah?
-Yeah.

571
00:24:27,007 --> 00:24:28,341
-[Mary] You got it?
-[Anna] I got it.

572
00:24:28,425 --> 00:24:30,051
-Uh-oh. I got the bag dirty.
-Yes.

573
00:24:30,135 --> 00:24:32,053
-[Mary] I'm here.
-Yay!

574
00:24:32,137 --> 00:24:33,847
-[Anna] Are you excited?
-Oh, my goodness. I am.

575
00:24:34,431 --> 00:24:35,515
Yay!

576
00:24:36,141 --> 00:24:38,185
-I'm, like, nervous a little bit.
-[all laughing]

577
00:24:38,268 --> 00:24:39,853
-A little bit.
-[Nicole] Mary?

578
00:24:39,936 --> 00:24:41,438
-Yeah.
-Have you done your showing yet?

579
00:24:41,521 --> 00:24:42,355
No, not yet.

580
00:24:42,439 --> 00:24:44,649
I cannot believe you're doing that today,
you crazy lady.

581
00:24:45,108 --> 00:24:46,610
You're a trooper, I'll give you that.

582
00:24:46,985 --> 00:24:49,321
So I get a call from Preston, 
another agent.

583
00:24:49,404 --> 00:24:53,408
And he wants to see
my Doheny listing today,

584
00:24:53,492 --> 00:24:55,285
which happens to be my wedding venue.

585
00:24:55,368 --> 00:24:57,954
I was like, "There's a wedding,
there's stuff set up every place."

586
00:24:58,038 --> 00:25:01,208
-You didn't tell him it was yours?
-No. No, um...

587
00:25:01,291 --> 00:25:03,668
Not exactly convenient timing,

588
00:25:03,752 --> 00:25:06,338
but I'm going to do it.

589
00:25:06,421 --> 00:25:08,298
I'm going to be there anyway, so...

590
00:25:08,924 --> 00:25:11,676
I can't let this wedding get 
in the way of work. [chuckles]

591
00:25:11,760 --> 00:25:14,554
I said it'd be better if you come,
like, tomorrow or Monday

592
00:25:14,638 --> 00:25:16,890
when things are taken down
and it'll probably show better.

593
00:25:16,973 --> 00:25:18,558
He said he's only in town today.

594
00:25:18,683 --> 00:25:21,144
-It's a big music producer...
-Okay.

595
00:25:21,228 --> 00:25:23,647
...and he really wants to see it, so...

596
00:25:23,730 --> 00:25:25,482
Well, the house shows well no matter what.

597
00:25:25,565 --> 00:25:26,942
I'm gonna be here so let's do it.

598
00:25:27,025 --> 00:25:29,528
If I sell it on my wedding day, boom.

599
00:25:29,653 --> 00:25:30,612
That'd be pretty cool.

600
00:25:30,695 --> 00:25:33,031
-[Mary sighs]
-[Nicole] Is Amanza still not here yet?

601
00:25:33,573 --> 00:25:34,491
I guess not.

602
00:25:35,075 --> 00:25:37,202
[Mary] To be fair,
she's got two kids in tow.

603
00:25:37,285 --> 00:25:39,287
[Nicole] Are you enjoying the day?
Chilling?

604
00:25:39,371 --> 00:25:41,873
I'm a little, like, shaky, I think, but...

605
00:25:41,957 --> 00:25:45,961
[Nicole] Remember we're all here for you,
so timeline just doesn't matter.

606
00:25:46,044 --> 00:25:47,837
-Just relax.
-[Anna] Yeah.

607
00:25:47,921 --> 00:25:50,423
[Mary] Okay, guys,
I'm gonna go put that robe on.

608
00:25:55,887 --> 00:25:59,182
-[Amanza] I'm here!
-This, um, is the vows.

609
00:25:59,849 --> 00:26:02,060
-[Mary] I need a drink.
-[Nicole] I got you.

610
00:26:02,143 --> 00:26:04,938
-[champagne cork pops]
-Oh, look at your robe. So cute.

611
00:26:05,397 --> 00:26:07,148
-Hi.
-Hi, hon. How are you?

612
00:26:07,232 --> 00:26:08,108
Good. How are you?

613
00:26:08,191 --> 00:26:10,360
[Mary] I really am getting
a little, like...

614
00:26:11,778 --> 00:26:13,655
[inhales deeply, exhales]

615
00:26:13,738 --> 00:26:14,614
Oh, my God.

616
00:26:15,907 --> 00:26:17,784
-[Mary] I'm, like... stressing.
-Mary?

617
00:26:17,867 --> 00:26:20,036
[Amanza] Gotta break it a little
cause it's big.

618
00:26:20,120 --> 00:26:21,621
[knocking on door]

619
00:26:22,664 --> 00:26:23,915
-What...
-[Mary] Hi. Preston?

620
00:26:23,999 --> 00:26:25,542
-Hey, how's it going?
-[Mary] Hi!

621
00:26:25,625 --> 00:26:27,627
-How are you?
-Oh, my God, are you getting married?

622
00:26:27,711 --> 00:26:28,837
[Mary laughing] I am!

623
00:26:28,920 --> 00:26:30,839
-Congratulations.
-[Mary] Thank you.

624
00:26:30,922 --> 00:26:34,926
[Amanza] Only Mary.
This is the hardest working chick, like...

625
00:26:35,010 --> 00:26:37,429
It's your wedding day for the love of God.

626
00:26:37,512 --> 00:26:38,346
[Mary] I know,

627
00:26:38,430 --> 00:26:41,099
but I'm here anyway, 
so take a look around and then

628
00:26:41,182 --> 00:26:42,726
I'll run down there and meet you.

629
00:26:43,184 --> 00:26:44,769
-Okay?
-[Preston] Thank you. So sorry.

630
00:26:44,853 --> 00:26:46,354
No, don't be sorry.

631
00:26:49,149 --> 00:26:51,693
[Mary] How close are we
to a stopping point?

632
00:26:51,776 --> 00:26:53,695
I can just clip it here 
while you show them.

633
00:26:53,778 --> 00:26:54,654
[Mary] Okay.

634
00:26:56,740 --> 00:26:59,743
Okay. I'm going to go show him
this property really fast.

635
00:27:03,872 --> 00:27:05,915
[Mary] Hi! Sorry. Okay.

636
00:27:05,999 --> 00:27:07,459
So, yeah, it's a bit of a mess,

637
00:27:07,542 --> 00:27:11,004
-but I hope you see through everything.
-[Preston] This is awesome.

638
00:27:11,087 --> 00:27:13,923
All of this is Waterworks. 
La Cornue stove.

639
00:27:14,299 --> 00:27:15,717
-[Preston] Really nice.
-I know.

640
00:27:15,800 --> 00:27:18,762
-Isn't that stove incredible? Right?
-[cook] It's amazing.

641
00:27:19,137 --> 00:27:22,015
Okay, so, here is the formal living room.

642
00:27:23,600 --> 00:27:27,020
-The fireplace is imported from Italy.
-[Preston] That's cool.

643
00:27:27,103 --> 00:27:29,981
-Yeah, it is cool and the family room.
-Wow.

644
00:27:30,065 --> 00:27:31,941
French doors open up to the backyard.

645
00:27:34,903 --> 00:27:37,405
[Mary] The master bedroom is just amazing.

646
00:27:38,907 --> 00:27:40,825
All bedrooms have en-suite baths.

647
00:27:40,909 --> 00:27:43,370
The backyard is the selling point 
of the house.

648
00:27:43,453 --> 00:27:44,412
[Preston] Gorgeous!

649
00:27:44,496 --> 00:27:45,413
-Yeah.
-So nice.

650
00:27:45,497 --> 00:27:49,000
The pool is amazing. This guest house
over here has a kitchenette.

651
00:27:49,501 --> 00:27:50,919
Bathroom, shower...

652
00:27:51,002 --> 00:27:52,754
It's a studio, basically.

653
00:27:52,837 --> 00:27:53,880
Complete privacy.

654
00:27:53,963 --> 00:27:57,342
-[Preston] Amazing for a wedding too.
-[Mary] I know, I know.

655
00:27:57,425 --> 00:28:00,637
-Thank you again so much for showing me.
-Oh, my pleasure.

656
00:28:00,720 --> 00:28:03,056
-And we need to make the sale.
-[laughing] I know.

657
00:28:03,139 --> 00:28:04,891
I know, I plan to.

658
00:28:04,974 --> 00:28:09,479
This would be epic if I actually sell
my wedding venue on my wedding day.

659
00:28:09,562 --> 00:28:10,438
Love it.

660
00:28:14,693 --> 00:28:16,236
[Jason] Where's Romain, let's go, bud.

661
00:28:16,319 --> 00:28:17,362
-It's your wedding.
-I know.

662
00:28:17,445 --> 00:28:21,324
You sure you wanna go through this, bud?
To the last moment of being single, man.

663
00:28:21,408 --> 00:28:22,617
Been nice knowing you.

664
00:28:22,701 --> 00:28:25,829
-Does this look good?
-[Brett] Yeah, that's right.

665
00:28:25,912 --> 00:28:28,832
-Do you want the collar outside the vest?
-No, inside. God, you guys.

666
00:28:28,915 --> 00:28:30,792
Brett, you've clearly 
never modeled before.

667
00:28:39,092 --> 00:28:40,885
[Maya] Wow, this is beautiful.

668
00:28:41,678 --> 00:28:43,763
-I'm gonna fall. Can I have your arm?
-I know.

669
00:28:44,264 --> 00:28:45,390
[Jason] VIP couple.

670
00:28:46,099 --> 00:28:47,142
Hi, guys.

671
00:28:49,477 --> 00:28:51,271
-Hi, how are you?
-Hey, love.

672
00:28:51,354 --> 00:28:52,188
[Jason] Mwah.

673
00:28:53,732 --> 00:28:56,317
-[all] Cheers.
-Cheers to the bride and groom.

674
00:28:56,401 --> 00:28:58,403
[Christine] Give me a hug. Hi, honey!

675
00:28:59,404 --> 00:29:00,780
Hi, I'm Chrishell.

676
00:29:03,283 --> 00:29:04,993
[Mary] You guys look so nice.

677
00:29:05,076 --> 00:29:06,786
All of you guys look amazing.

678
00:29:06,870 --> 00:29:09,247
-[Steve] Not as nice as you.
-[Mary] Oh... Aw.

679
00:29:09,330 --> 00:29:10,623
You guys ready?

680
00:29:10,707 --> 00:29:12,709
-[Theresa] Yes.
-Yeah. We got this.

681
00:29:23,928 --> 00:29:25,263
-[Christine] Is this us?
-Yeah.

682
00:29:28,516 --> 00:29:29,976
I'm a little tipsy already.

683
00:29:30,059 --> 00:29:31,770
-[Maya] Are you?
-[Heather chuckles]

684
00:29:33,730 --> 00:29:35,815
Oh, you want it in the front? Sorry.

685
00:29:36,357 --> 00:29:37,734
-You want it in front?
-What?

686
00:29:37,817 --> 00:29:39,444
Your ponytail, I was gonna put it back.

687
00:29:39,944 --> 00:29:42,822
-I'm good, thanks.
-[Christine] I was fixing your hair!

688
00:29:42,906 --> 00:29:44,532
[laughing] Leave my hair alone.

689
00:29:44,616 --> 00:29:46,618
-No, I was fixing it.
-I'm gonna sit like this.

690
00:29:49,579 --> 00:29:50,872
[Chrishell] Oh, here they come.

691
00:29:51,247 --> 00:29:52,373
I love weddings.

692
00:29:53,249 --> 00:29:54,751
♪ They say ♪

693
00:29:55,335 --> 00:29:57,086
♪ Your heart speeds up ♪

694
00:29:57,170 --> 00:30:00,590
♪ And the world slows down ♪

695
00:30:02,300 --> 00:30:03,635
[Maya] That's Romain's Dad.

696
00:30:03,718 --> 00:30:04,761
Is that Mary's mom?

697
00:30:10,809 --> 00:30:14,062
♪ They say that you know ♪

698
00:30:14,812 --> 00:30:18,650
♪ Beyond a shadow of a doubt ♪

699
00:30:19,317 --> 00:30:22,821
♪ When you finally find ♪

700
00:30:23,780 --> 00:30:25,156
